### z.string()

Source: https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/blob/main/packages/docs/content/api.mdx

Creates a schema for string validation and transformation. Supports validation methods for length, regex, prefixes, suffixes, substrings, and casing, as well as transformation methods like trimming and normalization.

```APIDOC
### Function Signature
`z.string()`

### Validation Methods
- `.max(length: number)` - Validates maximum length (in Unicode code points).
- `.min(length: number)` - Validates minimum length (in Unicode code points).
- `.length(length: number)` - Validates exact length (in Unicode code points).
- `.nonempty()` - Alias for `.min(1)`.
- `.regex(pattern: RegExp)` - Validates that string matches regex pattern.
- `.startsWith(prefix: string)` - Validates string starts with prefix.
- `.endsWith(suffix: string)` - Validates string ends with suffix.
- `.includes(substring: string)` - Validates string contains substring.
- `.uppercase()` - Validates string is uppercase.
- `.lowercase()` - Validates string is lowercase.

### Transform Methods
- `.trim()` - Trims whitespace from string.
- `.toLowerCase()` - Converts string to lowercase.
- `.toUpperCase()` - Converts string to uppercase.
- `.normalize()` - Normalizes unicode characters.

### Examples
```ts
// Validations
z.string().max(5);
z.string().min(5);
z.string().length(5);
z.string().nonempty();
z.string().regex(/^[a-z]+$/);
z.string().startsWith("aaa");
z.string().endsWith("zzz");
z.string().includes("---");
z.string().uppercase();
z.string().lowercase();

// Unicode length handling
z.string().length(1).parse("😀"); // one code point, two UTF-16 units
z.string().length(2).parse("e\u0301"); // "é" — an e plus a combining acute
z.string().length(3).parse("🧑‍🍼"); // person + ZWJ + baby bottle

// Transforms
z.string().trim();
z.string().toLowerCase();
z.string().toUpperCase();
z.string().normalize();
```
```

