### Validate string constraints in Zod and Zod Mini

Source: https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/blob/main/packages/docs/content/api.mdx

Applies common string validation methods such as length limits, regular expressions, prefixes, suffixes, and casing checks. Zod Mini uses the .check() method with standalone validators.

```typescript
z.string().max(5);
z.string().min(5);
z.string().length(5);
z.string().nonempty(); // alias for .min(1)
z.string().regex(/^[a-z]+$/);
z.string().startsWith("aaa");
z.string().endsWith("zzz");
z.string().includes("---");
z.string().uppercase();
z.string().lowercase();
```

```typescript
z.string().check(z.maxLength(5));
z.string().check(z.minLength(5));
z.string().check(z.length(5));
z.string().check(z.minLength(1)); // alias for .nonempty()
z.string().check(z.regex(/^[a-z]+$/));
z.string().check(z.startsWith("aaa"));
z.string().check(z.endsWith("zzz"));
z.string().check(z.includes("---"));
z.string().check(z.uppercase());
z.string().check(z.lowercase());
```

