### Validate Unicode code point length with z.string().length

Source: https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/blob/main/packages/docs/content/api.mdx

Calculates string length using Unicode code points instead of UTF-16 code units. Non-BMP emoji count as a single code point, while combining characters and ZWJ sequences count as multiple code points.

```typescript
z.string().length(1).parse("😀"); // one code point, two UTF-16 units
z.string().length(2).parse("e\u0301"); // "é" — an e plus a combining acute
z.string().length(3).parse("🧑‍🍼"); // person + ZWJ + baby bottle
```

