### String length now counts code points

Source: https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/blob/main/packages/docs/content/blog/zod-4-5.mdx

.min(), .max(), and .length() now count Unicode code points instead of UTF-16 code units. .max() only loosens; .min() and .length() tighten for astral input, and graphemes are unchanged.

```ts
z.string().max(5).parse("😀😀😀😀😀"); // was too_big, now passes
z.string().min(5).parse("😀😀😀");     // was fine, now too_small
```

